   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the mental hygiene law, in relation to the establishment of\nthe independent intellectual and developmental disability ombudsman program",
    "basePrintNo": "S1766",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1766-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 42,
       "fullName": "Mike Martucci",
       "imgName": "1313_Mike_Martucci.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 1496,
       "sessionMemberId": 1851,
       "sessionYear": 2021,
       "shortName": "MARTUCCI"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §33.29, Ment Hyg L",
    "lawSection": "Mental Hygiene Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1766\n\nSPONSOR: MANNION\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the mental hygiene law, in relation to the establishment\nof the independent intellectual and developmental disability ombudsman\nprogram\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to ensure access to care for individuals\nwith an intellectual and/or developmental disability.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would establish the independent intellectual and developmental\ndisability ombudsman program. The Ombudsman's duties would include iden-\ntifying, investigating, referring and resolving complaints that are made\nbe, or on behalf of, consumers relative to coverage under a managed care\norganization and access to initial and continuing intellectual and\ndevelopmental disability services and supports as well as network\nadequacy for access to such services.\n\n \nSTATEMENT O SUPPORT:\n\nThe role of an ombudsman is essential in publicly funded human services\ndelivery systems and is especially vital when new systems are put in\nplace. An ombudsman is officially charged with representing the inter-\nests of the public and is independent from the government. A NYS\nSubstance Abuse Disorder and Mental Health Ombudsman was successfully\ncreated in the enacted budget for state fiscal year 2018-2019. It has\nhelped individuals and their families navigate New York's behavioral\nhealth care system to ensure people have access to necessary care and\nservices and resolve issues related to care being delayed or denied.\n\nNew York State continues to transition the I/DD programs into a managed\ncare service system. Throughout this transition, many I/DD service\nrecipients and their families have expressed concerns that their needs\nwill not be met and access to care will be diminished under a managed\ncare structure.\n\nThis bill would help to ensure access to appropriate levels of care\nwhich meet the specific needs of each service recipient with an intel-\nlectual or developmental disability by establishing an\nindependent/intellectual and developmental disability (I/DD) ombudsman\nprogram by protecting the rights of consumers.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS7716: Died in Committee\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nUndetermined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the one hundred eightieth day after it\nshall have become law.\n",
